{
  // audit-ci gates `npm audit` results in CI: fails the build on any new
  // high/critical vulnerability, per Master Plan Section 9/11's requirement
  // that a failing check blocks merge, not just warns.
  //
  // The 3 entries below are the ONLY currently-known exceptions, and this
  // allowlist is deliberately narrow — anything not listed here still fails
  // the build. All 3 are the same root cause: `multer` (a transitive
  // dependency of `@nestjs/platform-express`, pulled in only because Nest's
  // Express adapter depends on it — this app has no file-upload endpoint
  // anywhere and never calls multer directly; confirmed via
  // `grep -r "multer|FileInterceptor|UploadedFile" src/` returning nothing).
  // All 3 advisories are specifically about multipart/file-upload request
  // handling, so none are reachable through this app's actual attack
  // surface today. (A 4th multer advisory, GHSA-qvfw-j98x-7q72, is "low"
  // severity — already below this file's "high" gate on its own, so
  // audit-ci itself flags listing it here as unnecessary; deliberately left
  // out rather than allowlisted for no reason.) `npm audit fix --force`'s
  // only available fix is downgrading @nestjs/core from 11.2.3 to 7.5.5 —
  // four major versions back — which is not a viable fix. Revisit this
  // allowlist (and multer's version) the moment this app adds any
  // file-upload endpoint, or the moment @nestjs/platform-express bumps its
  // own multer dependency.
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": [
    "GHSA-wc9g-mqfw-jrwm",
    "GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf",
    "GHSA-535w-7cp7-47q4"
  ]
}
